.TH DRAFTPAPER 1 "2026-10-14" "draftpaper 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
draftpaper \- the i3 desktop drawn as a drafting sheet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B draftpaper
.RI start | stop | apply | theme " " [ list | next | NAME ] | park " " [ toggle | at " " CELL | next | prev | show " " ID ] | readings | version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Draftpaper replaces the i3 bar with a drafting sheet: a wallpaper with a frame, zone ticks and a dot grid,
a live title block carrying the readings, lettered margins, and side-margin cells for parked windows.
Include
.I /usr/share/draftpaper/i3/draftpaper.conf
from the i3 configuration; it runs
.B draftpaper start
and binds Super+Escape (park);
.I /usr/share/draftpaper/i3/draftpaper-cycle.conf
adds Super+Left/Right to cycle through parked windows (they replace i3's default focus keys).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Apply the theme and start the shell.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the shell.
.TP
.B apply
Re-render the sheet and the generated i3 and shell files after a change to the configuration.
.TP
.BR theme " [" list "|" next "|" \fINAME\fR]
List the themes, switch to the next one, or switch to NAME.
.TP
.BR park " " toggle "|" at " " \fICELL\fR "|" next "|" prev "|" show " " \fIID\fR
Park the focused window in the first free side-margin cell or in CELL (or bring every parked window back
on a workspace with none showing), cycle through the parked windows, or bring one back.
.TP
.B readings
Print the readings the shell polls, as JSON.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/draftpaper/config.toml
Settings: theme, margin, title block, a custom cell, alert thresholds, commands.
.TP
.I ~/.config/draftpaper/themes/
Themes of your own.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/draftpaper/
Generated sheets, theme.json and i3.conf.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR i3 (1),
.BR qs (1)
